er so for those of you that have  listened to content from me for a while  you know that i've been a big believer  that twitter and square will likely  merge at some point in the future and  the idea is that in the western world we  have yet to see  a super app built  from taking a leading financial company  and a leading communications company and  putting them together we have them in  the east in china and elsewhere but in  the west we have yet to see that really  happen and so the idea would be if you  take twitter and you combine it or merge  it with square you now would have a  public forum where conversation happens  in real time people have identity they  have connections a social graph etc and  you overlay it with financial services  that would allow you to pay merchants or  pay for goods and services to be able to  pay each other etc it's an interesting  idea  but all of a sudden when you take it  from the legacy infrastructure rails and  you bring it to the lightning network  which is the layer 2 for bitcoin  you realize that the lightning network  allows for something much much more  powerful the lightning network allows  anyone anywhere in the world to tap into  global infrastructure and send very  small amounts of money the equivalent of  pennies  to anyone else in the world  instantaneous and completely for free  why is that so important to something  like twitter well if you think about all  the financial services that could be  integrated into twitter  it's things around tipping joe has a  great tweet here's a penny or two penny  john  publishes something that i like  and i want to read it and he puts it  behind a paywall john here's 10 cents so  i could read your article micropayments  or  i want to listen to  a twitter spaces and joe and john are on  there roasting each other  maybe i could stream sats while i listen  to the twitter spaces so that they can  make some money while they're doing it  there are example after example after  example where these micro payments could  be super valuable  but you need infrastructure that can  actually process it and so when you  start to think about the legacy  infrastructure it actually is very  difficult to do micro payments it's  expensive and it's slow but when you use  the second layer of bitcoin something  like the lightning network it becomes  very viable and so if jack was actually  to go as far as to link every account on  twitter to a lightning wallet not only  would it serve as a massive inflection  point for both twitter and bitcoin but  it would push us much further  towards jack's vision of bitcoin  becoming a native currency for the  internet if you think of one of the  problems with currency  on the digital  kind of landscape  every fiat currency in the world has  been built to serve as the reserve  currency within a certain geographic  region so in the united states the u.s  economy has the u.s dollar in mexico the  mexican economy has the mexican peso etc  you can go around the world and see this  fiat currencies have been tied to  geographic boundaries and geographically  focused economies  but the digital economy  knows no bounds there is no geographic  boundaries when it comes to the digital  world i can enter into the portal of my  smartphone or my computer and i can  communicate and i can transact and i can  participate hang out with etc anyone  else in the world who also entered into  that digital world through the portal of  their phone or their computer and so if  now all of a sudden geography doesn't  matter  and the  individual  geographic based economies start to fade  into the background and the digital  economy becomes  ultimately the most important what is  the native currency of the internet what  is the native currency of that digital  economy there hasn't been one and that  ultimately is what jack dorsey's vision  for bitcoin is from what i understand  and so if that actually was to occur  now you don't have to worry about  exchange rates you don't have to worry  about multi-day settlement times you  don't have to worry about high cost of  transactions you simply can use bitcoin  and have everything denominated in  bitcoin and have anyone anywhere in the  world accept bitcoin pay in bitcoin  store their wealth in bitcoin etc  if bitcoin is able to rise to become the  global reserve currency of the digital  economy something like twitter being  able to link every single twitter  account to a lightning wallet  would be  an immense move forward for both the  company and the digital currency now  many people would say why the hell would  a big tech company or a centralized  entity like twitter be willing to  integrate with a decentralized digital  currency something they do not control  why would they want to plug into an open  network like this don't these large big  tech companies want control don't they  want to have centralization don't they  benefit from that both monetarily and  also from a implementation of their  vision of course  but jack dorsey is not your normal ceo  jack had a second tweet where somebody  said that big tech is scared of ethereum  ethereum disrupts big tech  and jack so eloquently just said  disrupting big tech is exactly what's  needed and what i want no one technology  alone will do that though and so what's  fascinating about this in my opinion  is that jack dorsey is the ceo of a big  tech company but he understands that we  need to disrupt it he understands the  innovator's dilemma he understands that  if he does not disrupt the current  twitter model then somebody else will  and so you continue to see him work on  things like blue sky which is a focus  of creating a decentralized version  and a decentralized protocol on which  social networks can be built on in the  future you see him focusing on things  like bitcoin which is a decentralized  digital currency and trying to figure  out how can he integrate it into a  service like twitter  jack dorsey understands where the world  is going and jack dorsey is trying to  disrupt himself  and that is usually a very very very  rare position for somebody with such  wealth and power and success to be in  because most people would just continue  to double and triple down on what's  working they would continue to try to  drive as much financial gain as possible  and continue to expand their control  over their mini fiefdom but jack dorsey  understands there's a bigger play in  other tweets that we don't have pulled  up he's basically talked about the fact  that it's not about the money he's going  to donate all the money anyways it's not  that that it drives him he simply wants  to create a better world he wants to  bring social and economic freedom to  people around the world he's not only  doing it in the united states he's  focused on other places like nigeria  ghana etc and  i'm willing to bet that jack dorsey is  going to end up using technology and  create immense leverage for him and his  team to be able to usher a lot of this  change in hey guys thanks so much for  watching that clip of the best business  show make sure you like and subscribe to  the channel turn on notifications so you  know when we go live every weekday and  then head to sofi.com so that you can  get an account we can get after it

